===Classification===
''Symphyotrichum pilosum'' is classified in [[subgenus]] ''Symphyotrichum'' [[Section (botany)|section]] ''Symphyotrichum'' [[Subsection (botany)|subsection]] ''Porteriani''. This subsection contains four species in addition to ''{{Nowrap|S. pilosum}}'': ''[[Symphyotrichum depauperatum|S.{{Nbsp}}depauperatum]]'' (serpentine aster), ''[[Symphyotrichum kentuckiense|S.{{Nbsp}}kentuckiense]]'' (Kentucky aster), ''[[Symphyotrichum parviceps|S.{{Nbsp}}parviceps]]'' (smallhead aster), and ''[[Symphyotrichum porteri|S.{{Nbsp}}porteri]]'' (Porter's aster). Two commonalities among the five species are their [[Revolute leaf|revolute]] [[Phyllary|phyllaries]] and their summer- and fall-forming [[Rosette (botany)|basal leaf rosettes]].{{Sfnp|Semple|2014c}}
