===Varieties===
[[File:Symphyotrichum pilosum pringlei 92057395 (cropped).jpg|thumb|right|upright=1|''Symphyotrichum pilosum'' var. ''pringlei'' in [[Rothrock State Forest]] near [[Huntingdon, Pennsylvania]]]]
Two varieties are accepted by ''[[Plants of the World Online]]'' (POWO).{{Sfnp|POWO|2022}} Determining the best taxonomy for this group has been difficult due to [[polyploidy]] and hybridization.{{Sfnp|Yatskievych|2009}} The two currently recognized varieties are
* {{Nowrap|''S.'' ''pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' ([[Autonym (botany)|autonym]]), with hairy stems and leaves, widespread, and often weedy;{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}} and,
* {{Nowrap|''S.'' ''pilosum'' var.}} ''pringlei'', commonly called {{Strong|Pringle's aster}}{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006b}} and named for American botanist [[Cyrus Guernsey Pringle]].{{Sfnp|Wilhelm|Rericha|2017|p=1105}}

===Hybridization===
Putative [[F1 hybrid|hybridization]] of ''Symphyotrichum'' {{Nowrap|''pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' with twelve species of the genus has been reported: ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum cordifolium|S. cordifolium]]}}'' (common blue wood aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum drummondii|S. drummondii]]}}'' (Drummond's aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum dumosum|S. dumosum]]}}'' (bushy aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum laeve|S. laeve]]}}'' (smooth aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum lanceolatum|S. lanceolatum]]}}'' (panicled aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum novi-belgii|S. novi-belgii]]}}'' (New York aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum oolentangiense|S. oolentangiense]]}}'' (skyblue aster),{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=860}} ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum parviceps|S. parviceps]]}}'' (smallhead aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum praealtum|S. praealtum]]}}'' (willowleaf aster), ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum racemosum|S. racemosum]]}}'' (small white aster),{{Sfnp|Yatskievych|2009}} ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum tradescantii|S. tradescantii]]}}'' (shore aster), and ''{{Nowrap|[[Symphyotrichum urophyllum|S. urophyllum]]}}'' (arrowleaf aster).{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=860}} Additionally, it has been determined that pollination has occurred between the two varieties or between the tetraploid and hexaploid cytotypes of {{Nowrap|''S. p.'' var.}} ''pilosum'' based on the discovery of pentaploids of that variety.{{Sfnp|Semple|Heard|Brouillet|2002|p=84}}

==Distribution==
===Native===
Both varieties of ''Symphyotrichum pilosum'' are [[Native plant|native]] to central and eastern [[Canada]] and the [[United States]], with the more common being {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} {{Nowrap|''pilosum''.{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}}{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006b}}}}

====Variety ''pilosum''====
Sources differ slightly on the distribution of {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum''. According to ''[[Flora of North America]]'' (FNA), it is native from west starting in [[Minnesota]], then east to [[Maine]], including [[Ontario]] and [[Québec]]; south along the [[Atlantic Seaboard]] including most southern and eastern states; the entire [[Midwest]]; the states bordering the [[Mississippi River]] except [[Louisiana]]; then with a northwest border to [[Arkansas]]; and, four [[Great Plains]] states, from south to north, [[Oklahoma]], [[Kansas]], [[Nebraska]], and [[South Dakota]]. States on the Atlantic Seaboard with no reported presence are [[Connecticut]], [[Delaware]], [[Maryland]], [[Rhode Island]], and [[Vermont]], plus [[West Virginia]]. FNA reports that it has been [[Introduced species|introduced]] to the Canadian provinces of [[British Columbia]], [[New Brunswick]], and [[Nova Scotia]].{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}}

POWO and [[NatureServe]] provide slightly different distribution information on this variety. According to POWO, it also is present in and native to Maryland, New Brunswick, and Nova Scotia. Like FNA, however, POWO reports that it is an introduced species in British Columbia.{{Sfnp|POWO|2022a}} NatureServe's map for {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' differs from FNA's with an additional introduced presence on [[Prince Edward Island]]; no presence in [[New Hampshire]], Nebraska, or South Dakota; and, a presence in Connecticut, Delaware, Louisiana, Maryland, Rhode Island, and {{Nowrap|[[Washington, D.C.]]{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022a}}}}

====Variety ''pringlei''====
{{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pringlei'' is an east-central and northeastern North American variety, and according to FNA and POWO, it is native to the area encompassing Minnesota in the northwest then east to Québec and Nova Scotia, in the United States on the Atlantic Seaboard south to [[North Carolina]], then northwest to [[Kentucky]], [[Illinois]], and then north to [[Wisconsin]].{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006b}}{{Sfnp|POWO|2022b}} NatureServe differs and includes a presence for this variety in Arkansas, [[Georgia (U.S. State)|Georgia]], [[South Carolina]], and [[Tennessee]].{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022b}}

