===Introduced===
{{As of|2022|November}}, {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' was reported by NatureServe as an [[introduced species]] in the Canadian provinces of [[British Columbia]], [[New Brunswick]], [[Nova Scotia]], and [[Prince Edward Island]];{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022a}} and, by POWO in the countries of Belgium, France, Germany, Great Britain, India, Italy, Korea, Netherlands, and Spain.{{Sfnp|POWO|2022a}} {{As of|2022|August}}, it was not on the European Union's [[List of invasive alien species of Union concern]].{{Sfnp|European Commission|2022}}

==Habitat==
===Variety ''pilosum'' habitat===
[[File:Symphyotrichum pilosum 166742870.jpg|thumb|upright=1|alt=refer to caption|{{Nowrap|''S. p.'' var.}} ''pilosum'' growing in the sand near [[Blue Marsh Lake]], [[Berks County, Pennsylvania]], United States]]
{{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' is tolerant of harsh growing conditions.{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} It usually is found at elevations between [[sea level]] and {{Convert|1000|m|ft|-2|abbr=off|sp=us}}{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}} in disturbed areas such as [[fallow]]ed land,{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} old fields, roadsides,{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}} salted roadsides, railroads, pastures,{{Sfnp|Wilhelm|Rericha|2017|p=1104}} [[landfill]]s, and [[Quarry|quarries]]. It occurs less frequently{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} in natural [[prairie]]s, open [[deciduous wood]]s,{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006a}} [[limestone]] [[outcrop]]s,{{Sfnp|Semple|2014}} and, very uncommonly, [[wetland]]s.{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} Hexaploids of this variety are usually founds in habitats that were once covered in [[glacier]]s.{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=856}}

===Variety ''pringlei'' habitat===
[[File:Symphyotrichum pilosum pringlei 92057489.jpg | thumb | upright=0.8 | alt=refer to caption |{{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pringlei'' at [[Rocky Ridge Natural Area]], [[Rothrock State Forest]], [[Huntingdon County, Pennsylvania]], United States, which has exposures of limestone and [[Ridgeley Sandstone|Oriskany sandstone]]{{Sfnp|DCNR|2022}}]]

{{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pringlei'' is common in [[Calcareous|calcium-rich]] [[ecosystem]]s such as [[calcareous grassland]]s and [[fen]]s,{{Sfnp|Wilhelm|Rericha|2017|p=1105}} limestone [[alvar]]s,{{Sfnp|Semple|2014b}} [[shale]] outcrops,{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} and [[Marl|marly]] {{Wikt-lang|en|panne|pannes|italic=no}}.{{Efn|group=n|name=marlypannes}}{{Sfnp|Wilhelm|Rericha|2017|p=1105}} It also has been found in various partially-sandy or sandy areas,{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} on [[moraine]] [[cliff]]s along lakes in woodland openings, and in environments similar to these.{{Sfnp|Wilhelm|Rericha|2017|p=1105}} It can be found in habitats attractive to {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' almost as equally as in the higher-quality ones previously mentioned.{{Sfnp|Chmielewski|Semple|2001|p=857}} Elevations of occurrences are from [[sea level]] to {{Convert|1100|m|ft|-2|abbr=off|sp=us}}, sometimes higher.{{Sfnp|Brouillet|Semple|Allen|Chambers|2006b}}

===Wetland indicator statuses===
[[File:Symphyotrichum pilosum WISRs WetlandRegionsMap-2016.png|thumb|upright=0.8|alt=refer to caption and text|[[US Army Corps of Engineers]] wetland regions map (2016) labeled with the 2020 wetland indicator status ratings for {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum''{{Sfnp|CRREL|2020|p=158}}}}]]
{{Nowrap|''Symphyotrichum pilosum''}} is categorized on the United States National Wetland Plant List (NWPL) with the [[Wetland indicator status|wetland indicator status rating]] of [[:wikt:facultative|Facultative]] (FAC) in the [[Wetland region (United States)|Atlantic and Gulf Coastal Plain]] (AGCP) and the Eastern Mountains and Piedmont (EMP) regions. The FAC rating means that {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum''}} is likely to occur either in wetlands or non-wetlands. It is categorized Facultative Upland (FACU) in the Arid West (AW), Great Plains (GP), Midwest (MW), Northcentral and Northeast (NCNE), and Western Mountains, Valleys, and Coast (WMVC) regions. Rating FACU means that it usually occurs in non-wetlands within its range, but can occasionally be found in wetlands.{{Sfnp|CRREL|2020|p=158}}

==Conservation==
[[NatureServe]] lists the species and its varieties with various [[NatureServe conservation status|conservation statuses]], and some states and provinces within range do not have statuses. {{As of|2022|November}}, {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum''}} was listed as Globally Secure (G5); and, State Secure (S5) in [[Ontario]], [[Delaware]], Georgia, [[Iowa]], [[Mississippi]], [[New York state|New York]], [[North Carolina]], [[Virginia]], and [[West Virginia]].{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022}}

{{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pilosum'' was listed as a Globally Secure Variety (T5); Secure (S5) in Ontario, Delaware, Georgia, [[New Jersey]], New York, Virginia, and West Virginia; and, Vulnerable (S3) in Québec and Minnesota.{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022a}} {{Nowrap|''S. pilosum'' var.}} ''pringlei'' also was listed as a Globally Secure Variety (T5); Secure (S5) in Delaware, New Jersey, and Virginia; Apparently Secure (S4) in Ontario and New York; Vulnerable (S3) in Minnesota; Imperiled (S2) in Québec and West Virginia; and, Critically Imperiled (S1) in Arkansas.{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022b}} The global statuses were last reviewed in 2016.{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022}}{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022a}}{{Sfnp|NatureServe|2022b}}

==Cultivation==
''Symphyotrichum pilosum'' var. ''pringlei''{{Sfnp|Royal Horticultural Society|n.d.a}} and its [[cultivar]] 'Ochtendgloren'{{Sfnp|Royal Horticultural Society|n.d.b}} have both won the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].{{Sfnp|Royal Horticultural Society|2017}}

